iThis is the simple menu format
1Go Back	./home.sm
i
i 1: File structure
iLike gopher, each sm file is one or more lines
iEach line is a menu entry, and each line's first character is the type
iAfter the type, it includes a tab separated list of arguments for the type
i 2: Types
iThese are the characters you can use as types
i [i] Information
iThis type means that the menu item is text, which is to be displayed in the menu
iIf you leave no text after the type, it will render as a horizontal rule
i [h] HTTP Hyperlink
iThis type means that the menu item is an HTTP Hyperlink
iWhen the user clicks on the menu item, it should navagate to the destination
iThe arguments of this item are as so: [Name] and [Link]
i Example: hName of link[TAB]Hyperlink[New line]
i [1] Menu
iThis type means that the menu item is a link to another menu
iThe arguments of this item are as so: [Text] and [Link]
i [p] Picture
iThis type means that the menu item is an image
iThe arguments of this item are as so: [Image URL] and [Alt Text]
iIf no alt text is provided, then the image should render anyway
i [b] Header
iThis type means that the menu item is a Header, same as i but with bigger text
i [e] Error
iThis type means that the server has encountered an error, same as i but with an error indication
i [j] Javascript
iThis type executrs a javascript expression and replaces the item's content with it
i
1See a sample here	./sample.sm
